{"claims":[{"id":"G1","kind":"goal","description":"After a snapshot is durably persisted and log compaction completes, a restarted or lagging Raft peer must retain a recoverable representation of the committed FSM state and the history needed for continued replication.","source_ids":["README.md:1:100","docs/README.md:1:100","snapshot.go:15:278"],"scope":{"description":"Snapshot creation, persistence, compaction, snapshot installation, and recovery for the configured SnapshotStore and LogStore.","assumptions":["The configured snapshot store and log store satisfy their interfaces.","Crash and storage-error behavior of concrete stores is not supplied."],"excluded":["FSM application determinism beyond the supplied FSM interface contract.","Concrete filesystem or database atomicity guarantees."],"parameters":[]},"pending":["Concrete store durability and recovery semantics are unread."],"grounding":{"behavior_ids":["snapshot.go:15:278","replication.go:137:387"],"expectation_ids":["README.md:1:100","docs/README.md:1:100","fsm.go:16:285"],"binding_ids":["B1","B2","B3","B4"],"derivation":"The implementation persists an FSM snapshot, records snapshot metadata, compacts logs, and later sends a snapshot to lagging peers. The documentation states that snapshots permit removal of logs used to reach the captured state and that committed entries may be applied to the FSM.","applicability":"Applicable when snapshotting is enabled, a snapshot is successfully created and persisted, and compaction or lagging-peer recovery is exercised.","unresolved":["Whether concrete store implementations make persisted snapshot data and metadata durable together.","Whether recovery reconstructs all state required after the selected compaction point."],"conflicts":[],"alternatives":["The selected store may provide stronger atomicity or recovery guarantees than the interfaces express."]}},{"id":"O1","kind":"obligation","description":"For every successful takeSnapshot path, log deletion must not remove the only recoverable history or snapshot representation needed to reconstruct the FSM state at or before the compacted index and to continue replication.","source_ids":["snapshot.go:15:278","replication.go:137:387"],"scope":{"description":"The successful path from Raft.takeSnapshot through SnapshotSink.Close, last-snapshot publication, compactLogs, and later sendLatestSnapshot.","assumptions":["The snapshot metadata index identifies the state represented by the persisted snapshot.","The configured LogStore and SnapshotStore implement the documented interface semantics."],"excluded":["Failure behavior of concrete stores not included in the supplied materials.","Concurrent snapshot deletion or external store mutation."],"parameters":[]},"pending":["The source for concrete store Close, List ordering, Open durability, and DeleteRange behavior is missing.","The restart reconstruction path is missing."],"grounding":{"behavior_ids":["snapshot.go:15:278","replication.go:137:387"],"expectation_ids":["README.md:1:100","docs/README.md:1:100","snapshot.go:15:278"],"binding_ids":["B1","B2","B3","B4"],"derivation":"takeSnapshot calls FSMSnapshot.Persist, closes the sink, updates last-snapshot state, and then compacts through compactLogsWithTrailing. A lagging peer is later recovered through sendLatestSnapshot, which selects and opens a listed snapshot. These producer-consumer dependencies make recoverability across compaction an applicable candidate obligation.","applicability":"Applicable only after successful snapshot persistence and close; not established for error paths or concrete stores whose contracts are unread.","unresolved":["Whether sink.Close durably publishes the snapshot before compaction.","Whether List returns a snapshot that Open can still recover after compaction.","Whether the FSM snapshot is semantically complete at snapReq.index."] ,"conflicts":[],"alternatives":["TrailingLogs may preserve sufficient incremental history even if snapshot recovery is unavailable, but this is not established."]}}],"bindings":[{"associations":[{"claim_id":"G1","source_ids":["snapshot.go:15:278"],"rationale":"SnapshotStore and snapshot orchestration define the persisted snapshot and compaction boundary relevant to recoverability."},{"claim_id":"O1","source_ids":["snapshot.go:15:278"],"rationale":"takeSnapshot and compactLogsWithTrailing implement the deletion boundary."}],"anchor":{"source_ids":["snapshot.go:15:278"],"boundary_complete":true,"kind":"declaration","material_id":"snapshot.go:15:278","start_line":125,"end_line":211,"symbol":"Raft.takeSnapshot"},"id":"B1","material_id":"snapshot.go:15:278","symbol":"Raft.takeSnapshot","start_line":125,"end_line":211,"description":"Requests an FSM snapshot, obtains committed configuration, persists it through SnapshotSink, publishes last-snapshot state, and invokes log compaction.","pending":["Concrete SnapshotSink durability is external."]},{"associations":[{"claim_id":"O1","source_ids":["snapshot.go:15:278"],"rationale":"This declaration computes the deletion range and invokes LogStore.DeleteRange."}],"anchor":{"source_ids":["snapshot.go:15:278"],"boundary_complete":true,"kind":"declaration","material_id":"snapshot.go:15:278","start_line":216,"end_line":248,"symbol":"Raft.compactLogsWithTrailing"},"id":"B2","material_id":"snapshot.go:15:278","symbol":"Raft.compactLogsWithTrailing","start_line":216,"end_line":248,"description":"Computes the compacted range from snapshot index, last log index, and configured trailing logs, then deletes that range.","pending":["LogStore.DeleteRange semantics are not supplied."]},{"associations":[{"claim_id":"O1","source_ids":["snapshot.go:15:278"],"rationale":"The interface defines the external snapshot publication, listing, and reopening operations consumed by replication."}],"anchor":{"source_ids":["snapshot.go:15:278"],"boundary_complete":true,"kind":"interface_member","material_id":"snapshot.go:15:278","start_line":49,"end_line":59,"symbol":"SnapshotStore"},"id":"B3","material_id":"snapshot.go:15:278","symbol":"SnapshotStore","start_line":49,"end_line":59,"description":"External snapshot store contract for create, ordered listing, and reopening persisted snapshots.","pending":["Concrete implementation and durability contract are unread."]},{"associations":[{"claim_id":"G1","source_ids":["replication.go:137:387"],"rationale":"This behavior opens the selected snapshot and transmits its metadata and contents to a lagging peer."},{"claim_id":"O1","source_ids":["replication.go:137:387"],"rationale":"Recovery after compaction depends on this consumer being able to open a usable snapshot."}],"anchor":{"source_ids":["replication.go:137:387"],"boundary_complete":true,"kind":"declaration","material_id":"replication.go:137:387","start_line":299,"end_line":383,"symbol":"Raft.sendLatestSnapshot"},"id":"B4","material_id":"replication.go:137:387","symbol":"Raft.sendLatestSnapshot","start_line":299,"end_line":383,"description":"Lists snapshots, opens the most recent one, sends it to a follower, and advances follower replication state on success.","pending":["Follower installation and restart recovery behavior are unread."]}],"relations":[{"id":"R1","source":"G1","target":"O1","kind":"depends_all","group":null,"rationale":"The recoverability goal requires the compaction boundary to preserve a usable recovery representation.","pending":[],"grounding":{"behavior_ids":["snapshot.go:15:278","replication.go:137:387"],"expectation_ids":["README.md:1:100","docs/README.md:1:100"],"binding_ids":["B1","B2","B4"],"derivation":"The goal's consequence is realized through the successful snapshot-to-compaction-to-recovery path.","applicability":"Applicable to snapshot-enabled recovery and lagging-peer catch-up.","unresolved":[],"conflicts":[],"alternatives":[]}},{"id":"R2","source":"O1","target":"B1","kind":"boundary","group":null,"rationale":"O1 depends on takeSnapshot establishing the persisted snapshot and the exact index before deletion.","pending":["Snapshot publication durability remains unverified."],"grounding":{"behavior_ids":["snapshot.go:15:278"],"expectation_ids":["snapshot.go:15:278"],"binding_ids":["B1"],"derivation":"The producer behavior is the snapshot persistence and publication sequence preceding compaction.","applicability":"Applicable on the successful takeSnapshot path.","unresolved":["Whether Close makes data durable before subsequent deletion."],"conflicts":[],"alternatives":[]}},{"id":"R3","source":"O1","target":"B4","kind":"boundary","group":null,"rationale":"O1 depends on a later consumer being able to list and open the retained snapshot for a lagging peer.","pending":["Snapshot installation and restart reconstruction are not supplied."],"grounding":{"behavior_ids":["replication.go:137:387"],"expectation_ids":["README.md:1:100"],"binding_ids":["B4"],"derivation":"sendLatestSnapshot is the observed recovery consumer for a follower whose log is too far behind.","applicability":"Applicable when replication reaches ErrLogNotFound and a snapshot exists.","unresolved":["Whether the opened snapshot contains all state required by the consumer."],"conflicts":[],"alternatives":[]}}],"units":[{"audit_question":{"disposition":"needs_specific_evidence","preferred_check":"source_review","requests":[{"file":"file_snapshot.go","start_line":1,"end_line":551,"reason":"Inspect concrete snapshot creation, close, listing order, open, deletion, and recovery durability behavior."},{"file":"inmem_snapshot.go","start_line":1,"end_line":113,"reason":"Determine whether the available in-memory implementation can establish snapshot publication and open semantics for a local check."},{"file":"raft.go","start_line":1244,"end_line":1602,"reason":"Trace commit-to-FSM scheduling and response correlation needed to establish what snapshot index represents."},{"file":"raft.go","start_line":1603,"end_line":1955,"reason":"Trace snapshot installation and recovery state reconstruction after a lagging peer receives a snapshot."}],"question":"Does the concrete configured SnapshotStore make a successfully closed snapshot durably openable, and does the restart or lagging-peer recovery path reconstruct the FSM state before compactLogsWithTrailing deletes the selected log range?","importance":"A failure could make committed state unrecoverable after compaction or prevent a lagging peer from rejoining, despite the documented snapshot-based bounded-log guarantee.","source_ids":["snapshot.go:15:278","replication.go:137:387","README.md:1:100","docs/README.md:1:100"],"participants":["leader Raft","lagging follower","FSM","SnapshotStore","LogStore"],"objects":["snapshot","committed log range","FSM state","follower replication state"],"contexts":["successful snapshot persistence","log compaction with configured TrailingLogs","ErrLogNotFound snapshot catch-up","restart or recovery"],"event_paths":["Raft.takeSnapshot: request FSM snapshot -> SnapshotSink.Persist -> SnapshotSink.Close -> setLastSnapshot -> compactLogs","Raft.compactLogsWithTrailing: compute maxLog -> LogStore.DeleteRange","Raft.sendLatestSnapshot: SnapshotStore.List -> Open -> InstallSnapshot -> nextIndex=meta.Index+1"],"points":[{"sequence_required":true,"id":"CP1","phase":"establish","source_ids":["snapshot.go:15:278"],"binding_ids":["B1"],"claim_ids":["O1"],"question":"Is the snapshot fully persisted and durably visible before compaction begins?","unknowns":["Concrete SnapshotSink.Close semantics"]},{"sequence_required":true,"id":"CP2","phase":"use","source_ids":["snapshot.go:15:278"],"binding_ids":["B2"],"claim_ids":["O1"],"question":"Which exact inclusive log range is deleted for the snapshot index and TrailingLogs configuration?","unknowns":["Concrete DeleteRange behavior and error durability"]},{"sequence_required":true,"id":"CP3","phase":"recover","source_ids":["replication.go:137:387"],"binding_ids":["B4"],"claim_ids":["G1","O1"],"question":"Can the retained snapshot be opened and applied to reconstruct the state needed after the deleted range?","unknowns":["Installation and restart reconstruction source"]}],"trigger_rationale":"First obtain the concrete store and recovery implementations. Then perform a local source-backed trace or direct test that persists a snapshot, compacts the selected range, reopens or installs the snapshot, and compares the reconstructed state and next replication index with the documented oracle. No deterministic asynchronous schedule is currently available."},"code_uses":[{"binding_id":"B1","role":"direct","claim_ids":["G1","O1"],"relation_ids":["R1","R2"],"source_ids":["snapshot.go:15:278"],"rationale":"The unit checks the snapshot persistence and compaction sequence.","unverified":["SnapshotStore durability"]},{"binding_id":"B2","role":"direct","claim_ids":["O1"],"relation_ids":["R1"],"source_ids":["snapshot.go:15:278"],"rationale":"The unit checks the deletion boundary.","unverified":["DeleteRange recovery impact"]},{"binding_id":"B4","role":"support","claim_ids":["G1","O1"],"relation_ids":["R3"],"source_ids":["replication.go:137:387"],"rationale":"The unit uses snapshot installation as the recovery consumer.","unverified":["Follower installation and restart behavior"]}],"coverage_intent":[{"sequence_required":true,"id":"CP1","phase":"establish","source_ids":["snapshot.go:15:278"],"binding_ids":["B1"],"claim_ids":["O1"],"question":"Snapshot persistence must precede deletion with a usable retained representation.","unknowns":["Concrete store durability"]},{"sequence_required":true,"id":"CP2","phase":"handoff","source_ids":["snapshot.go:15:278"],"binding_ids":["B2","B4"],"claim_ids":["G1","O1"],"question":"The deleted range must be recoverable through the retained snapshot or explicitly preserved trailing logs.","unknowns":["Concrete recovery path"]}],"id":"U1","goal_ids":["G1"],"obligation_ids":["O1"],"binding_ids":["B1","B2","B4"],"relation_ids":["R1","R2","R3"],"scope":{"description":"Snapshot persistence, compaction, and lagging-peer recovery for one configured store variant.","assumptions":["Only supplied source ranges are treated as observed behavior.","Concrete store and restart behavior remain deferred until requested reads are acquired."],"excluded":["Election and leadership transfer.","Application-level FSM determinism beyond the interface contract.","Other snapshot store variants not selected for investigation."],"parameters":[]},"rationale":"This is the highest-ranked feasible unit because it connects an explicit system consequence to a complete visible orchestration path, while the unresolved store and recovery handoffs are concrete and discriminating.","goal_observable":true}],"conflicts":["The supplied documentation describes snapshots as enabling safe log removal, but the supplied interfaces do not specify atomic durability or restart recovery semantics for concrete stores.","The supplied material shows snapshot orchestration and transmission but does not establish that the FSM snapshot represents exactly the state implied by snapReq.index."],"unexplored":["Client log admission and commit-to-FSM scheduling.","Vote and pre-vote response ownership across campaign contexts.","Configuration activation and quorum changes.","Leadership transfer and authority-loss handling.","Concrete FSM restore and follower snapshot-installation behavior."],"gaps":["Initial reading left the leader loop, client dispatch, AppendEntries handling, configuration implementation, and snapshot installation ranges deferred.","No precise asynchronous schedule replay capability is available.","No concrete store implementation evidence was acquired for durability, listing order, Open, Close, or DeleteRange."],"understanding":"The supplied implementation shows a snapshot thread obtaining an FSM snapshot, persisting and closing a sink, updating last-snapshot state, then compacting logs. Replication falls back to the latest listed snapshot when a follower is too far behind. The central unresolved boundary is whether the concrete store and recovery path preserve and reconstruct the required state across compaction or restart.","selection_rationale":"Selected snapshot persistence-to-compaction-to-recovery because it has a direct safety consequence, visible producer and consumer code, and a bounded evidence request. The result is intentionally provisional and not exhaustive.","reading_requests":[{"file":"file_snapshot.go","start_line":1,"end_line":551,"reason":"Inspect concrete snapshot lifecycle and storage recovery behavior."},{"file":"raft.go","start_line":1603,"end_line":1955,"reason":"Inspect snapshot installation and recovery state updates."},{"file":"raft.go","start_line":1244,"end_line":1602,"reason":"Inspect commit and FSM-index establishment before snapshot capture."}],"responsibilities":[{"id":"RESP1","description":"FSM snapshot capture and persistence","source_ids":["fsm.go:16:285","snapshot.go:15:278"],"entry_points":["Raft.takeSnapshot","Raft.runFSM"],"claim_ids":["G1","O1"],"handoffs":[{"covered_by_unit_ids":["U1"],"no_separate_check_reason":"The selected unit checks the persistence-to-compaction handoff and retains the unresolved FSM-index dependency.","target_id":"RESP2","source_ids":["snapshot.go:15:278"],"description":"Persisted snapshot metadata and bytes are handed to compaction and later recovery."}],"questions":["Does the snapshot capture represent the intended FSM index?","Does sink close publish durable, reopenable state?"],"applicability":"Applicable when snapshotting is enabled and the FSM has applied entries.","version":1},{"id":"RESP2","description":"Log compaction and snapshot-based follower catch-up","source_ids":["snapshot.go:15:278","replication.go:137:387"],"entry_points":["Raft.compactLogsWithTrailing","Raft.sendLatestSnapshot"],"claim_ids":["G1","O1"],"handoffs":[{"covered_by_unit_ids":["U1"],"no_separate_check_reason":"The same bounded unit checks the deletion boundary and the visible snapshot consumer.","target_id":"RESP3","source_ids":["replication.go:137:387"],"description":"A retained snapshot is handed to the follower installation path."}],"questions":["Can compaction remove data before recovery has a usable alternative?","Does snapshot installation restore the required replication position?"],"applicability":"Applicable when a follower is behind the retained log range or after restart.","version":1},{"id":"RESP3","description":"FSM application and restore","source_ids":["fsm.go:16:285"],"entry_points":["Raft.runFSM","FSM.Restore","FSM.Snapshot"],"claim_ids":[],"handoffs":[],"questions":["How are restored indexes and application state reconstructed?","What concrete FSM and snapshot implementation guarantees apply?"],"applicability":"Meaning is partially clear from interfaces, but the concrete restore path is not supplied.","version":1}],"exploration_requests":[{"reason":"The current workset does not represent client admission, commit progression, and completion correlation, which determine what state snapshot capture is expected to include.","responsibility_ids":["RESP3"],"requests":[{"file":"raft.go","start_line":468,"end_line":760,"reason":"Read leader-loop commit and replication responsibility."},{"file":"raft.go","start_line":1244,"end_line":1602,"reason":"Read client dispatch, persistence, commit scheduling, and AppendEntries handling."}]},{"reason":"Concrete store behavior is required to decide whether the snapshot-compaction obligation applies as an executable check.","responsibility_ids":["RESP1","RESP2"],"requests":[{"file":"file_snapshot.go","start_line":1,"end_line":551,"reason":"Read concrete snapshot store lifecycle and recovery behavior."},{"file":"inmem_snapshot.go","start_line":1,"end_line":113,"reason":"Read the local in-memory snapshot implementation and its limitations."}]}]}
